.TH HUNCHO 1 "October 2026" "huncho 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
huncho \- portable serving engine for System One decision models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B huncho
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B huncho
is a portable serving engine for Jev-style "System One" decision models. It
takes a state and a set of typed questions and returns calibrated probabilities
without text generation. It implements the Jev wire contract, so an unmodified
Python SDK works against it with only a base-URL change.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the HTTP API (\fI/v1/systemone\fR, \fI/health\fR, \fI/v1/models\fR,
\fI/metrics\fR). Serves a built-in mock model with
.BR --mock ,
or real manifests (\fB--manifest\fR) and Hugging Face model references
(\fB--model\fR).
.TP
.B convert
Convert model artifacts into a huncho model package (manifest + head + files).
.TP
.B calibrate
Fit calibration temperatures/confidence against golden vectors.
.TP
.B conform
Compare a backend against golden vectors and gate on probability fidelity,
argmax agreement, and ECE drift.
.TP
.B bench
Run a throughput/latency benchmark.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HUNCHO_BIND
Listener address (host:port), default \fI127.0.0.1:8080\fR.
.TP
.B HUNCHO_AUTH_TOKEN
Optional bearer token required on requests.
.TP
.B HUNCHO_BACKEND
Backend override for manifests/models: \fIauto\fR (default, selected per model),
\fIonnx\fR, \fIcandle\fR, \fIclef\fR, or \fImock\fR.
.TP
.B HUNCHO_DTYPE
Override the model-specific default dtype.
.TP
.B HUNCHO_CLEF_DEVICE
Clef device: \fIauto\fR (default) tries CUDA on GPU 0 and falls back to CPU.
Use \fIcpu\fR to force CPU, or \fIcuda\fR / \fIcuda:N\fR to require a GPU
and report an error if it is unavailable. CUDA requires a compatible NVIDIA
GPU, driver and runtime libraries; CPU needs no NVIDIA libraries.
.TP
.B HUNCHO_CACHE_DIR
Model cache directory, also used by Hugging Face resolution.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/huncho/huncho.env
Environment file read by the packaged systemd unit.
.TP
.I /usr/share/huncho/examples/mock-model
Bundled reference model package for testing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5)
